  "description": "Epoched stereo-EEG (157 contacts, 200 Hz, 588 trials) from a single patient with post-traumatic stress disorder, recorded during a face interpretation-bias task before and after SEEG-guided radiofrequency ablation of the right amygdala. The data are a BIDS derivative repackaging of the de-identified signals, event markers and channel annotations released by the authors on OSF. They support analysis of amygdala-related neural activity changes associated with reduced negative interpretation bias and symptoms.",
  "methods_description": "Stereo-EEG was recorded from one PTSD patient during a face interpretation-bias task in pre-ablation and post-ablation sessions. Epochs span -0.5 to 0.795 s (260 samples at 200 Hz) and were repackaged into BrainVision float32 files per session. Contact coordinates and anatomical labels come from the released channel information.",
